speechtext:
That is a very strange point of order. Let me get back to the Hon. Member for Broadview-Greenwood. Her Party has a resolution which has not changed, going back to 1961, which the NDP still confirms is its policy on trade. Let me indicate to this House and to the people of Canada what the policy is of the New Democratic Party in terms of trade. It is very clearly spelled out and it is exactly what has happened in this agreement. Let us remind Canadians of this. It states:
Expansion of our trade with any and all countries willing to trade on a fair and equitable basis will benefit both ourselves and them. Careful planning is needed to adjust our production to the trade requirements of a fully employed economy. Tariffs are outmoded patchwork attempts to protect domestic industry;
That is what this agreement does. It reduces tariffs.
